    "body": "## Problem\n\n`param-type-mismatch` is disabled for the Lua runtime, leaving argument type mismatches unchecked.\n\n## Solution\n\nEnable the diagnostic after correcting runtime annotations and calls, validating inputs, and adding local workarounds for checker limitations.\n\nThe first two commits isolate the EditorConfig root handling fix and API command/completion type corrections. The final commit contains the remaining runtime fixes and enables the check.\n\nTargeted functional tests, generated documentation, Lua/C style checks, and commit-message checks passed. The full EmmyLua check passed before rebasing, but the latest run reports the recurring `start_col` warning at `runtime/lua/vim/_core/ui2/messages.lua:422` (`expected integer but found nil`).\n",
    "closed_at": "2026-09-30T08:29:34Z",
